{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"R-18:87\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The passage sets the barrier beside another mode of Dhū al-Qarnayn’s rule: he says wrongdoers will be punished, then answers a people threatened by corrupters by building protection.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:87\",\"ar\":\"أَمَّا مَن ظَلَمَ فَسَوْفَ نُعَذِّبُهُۥ ثُمَّ يُرَدُّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّهِۦ فَيُعَذِّبُهُۥ عَذَابًۭا نُّكْرًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:94\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ يَأْجُوجَ وَمَأْجُوجَ مُفْسِدُونَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"ءَاتُونِى زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The same ruler moves from judgment of wrong to a practical response to the people’s stated danger.\",\"limits\":\"The text does not call the barrier a punishment or explicitly connect the two episodes as one policy.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:88\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The ruler who promises believers an easy course later refuses the people’s offer of payment and asks them to contribute strength to the barrier work.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:88\",\"ar\":\"وَسَنَقُولُ لَهُۥ مِنْ أَمْرِنَا يُسْرًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:94\",\"ar\":\"فَهَلْ نَجْعَلُ لَكَ خَرْجًا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"مَا مَكَّنِّى فِيهِ رَبِّى خَيْرٌۭ فَأَعِينُونِى بِقُوَّةٍ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both scenes show how Dhū al-Qarnayn deals with people under his rule.\",\"limits\":\"The believers in 18:88 are not identified with the people at the pass, and the verses do not state a common policy.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:89\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:90\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The eastern people have no screen from the sun, while the later people receive a constructed barrier against another danger; the sequence permits a contrast between exposure and protection.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:90\",\"ar\":\"لَّمْ نَجْعَل لَّهُم مِّن دُونِهَا سِتْرًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"أَجْعَلْ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ رَدْمًا\"}],\"missing\":\"The passage does not identify the two populations or equate a sun-screen with the barrier against Gog and Magog. A repeated protective term or an explicit link between the populations could establish the contrast more firmly.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:92\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The repeated formula ثُمَّ أَتْبَعَ سَبَبًا makes the barrier episode the endpoint of Dhū al-Qarnayn’s third journey; its material and labor instructions present that response as purposeful use of means.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:85\",\"ar\":\"فَأَتْبَعَ سَبَبًا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:89\",\"ar\":\"ثُمَّ أَتْبَعَ سَبَبًا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:92\",\"ar\":\"ثُمَّ أَتْبَعَ سَبَبًا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"ءَاتُونِى زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The third occurrence leads directly to his arrival at the pass and the staged work there.\",\"limits\":\"The text does not identify the iron or the people’s labor as the specific means named in ثُمَّ أَتْبَعَ سَبَبًا.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:93\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The repeated بين locates the work as closure of a particular gap: Dhū al-Qarnayn arrives between السدين, then levels the space between الصدفين.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:93\",\"ar\":\"بَيْنَ ٱلسَّدَّيْنِ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"سَاوَىٰ بَيْنَ ٱلصَّدَفَيْنِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both verses place Dhū al-Qarnayn between paired landforms at the same stage of the journey.\",\"limits\":\"The two nouns are not identical, so the wording does not establish that السدين and الصدفين are exact synonyms.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:94\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The focus answers a request for a سدّ between the people and the corrupters by specifying a rدم and its construction from iron, heat, and copper.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:94\",\"ar\":\"فَهَلْ نَجْعَلُ لَكَ خَرْجًا عَلَىٰٓ أَن تَجْعَلَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَهُمْ سَدًّۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"أَجْعَلْ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ رَدْمًا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"ءَاتُونِى زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The people’s offer and stated purpose immediately precede the focus’s material instructions.\",\"limits\":\"The verses do not explain a technical distinction between سدّ and ردم beyond using those terms for the requested and promised works.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:95\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The repeated plural commands in the focus enact the arrangement announced here: Dhū al-Qarnayn declines payment, asks for strength, and directs a cooperative build.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"مَا مَكَّنِّى فِيهِ رَبِّى خَيْرٌۭ فَأَعِينُونِى بِقُوَّةٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"ءَاتُونِى زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"قَالَ ٱنفُخُوا۟\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s repeated commands address a group and follow his request that they assist him.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not specify whether the helpers supply labor, tools, or both; it does not describe their payment arrangements beyond the declined offer.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:97\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The next verse states what the focus’s process achieves: the completed barrier cannot be climbed or pierced.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"أُفْرِغْ عَلَيْهِ قِطْرًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:97\",\"ar\":\"فَمَا ٱسْطَٰعُوٓا۟ أَن يَظْهَرُوهُ وَمَا ٱسْتَطَٰعُوا۟ لَهُۥ نَقْبًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The result follows immediately after the iron is heated and coated with molten metal.\",\"limits\":\"The verses report the barrier’s effect but do not specify its dimensions or how long it resists attack.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:98\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Dhū al-Qarnayn names the barrier mercy from his Lord and sets a limit to that protection: when the Lord’s promise comes, the barrier will be flattened.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:98\",\"ar\":\"هَٰذَا رَحْمَةٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّى\"},{\"ref\":\"18:98\",\"ar\":\"فَإِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ رَبِّى جَعَلَهُۥ دَكَّآءَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The pronoun هَٰذَا refers back to the barrier just built and tested in the preceding verses.\",\"limits\":\"The verse names the divine promise but does not specify its date or explain how the barrier will be flattened.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:99\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The surge in 18:99 follows the barrier’s appointed collapse, and 21:96 describes Gog and Magog being released and streaming down; the sequence may connect the wall’s end to their emergence.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:98\",\"ar\":\"فَإِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ رَبِّى جَعَلَهُۥ دَكَّآءَ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:99\",\"ar\":\"يَمُوجُ فِى بَعْضٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"21:96\",\"ar\":\"حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فُتِحَتْ يَأْجُوجُ وَمَأْجُوجُ وَهُم مِّن كُلِّ حَدَبٍۢ يَنسِلُونَ\"}],\"missing\":\"18:99 does not name the groups surging into one another, and 21:96 does not explicitly identify its opening with the flattening in 18:98. An explicit identification or a closer shared description of the event could settle the link.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-18:110\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-19:21\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-21:80\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The focus’s barrier and the armor-making in 21:80 are two forms of defensive manufacture: one protects a people from attack, the other protects bodies from battle.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"ءَاتُونِى زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ\"},{\"ref\":\"21:80\",\"ar\":\"وَعَلَّمْنَٰهُ صَنْعَةَ لَبُوسٍۢ لَّكُمْ لِتُحْصِنَكُم مِّنۢ بَأْسِكُمْ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s ironwork is built to answer the people’s request for protection from corrupters.\",\"limits\":\"21:80 does not name iron, and the verses do not say that Dhū al-Qarnayn’s barrier was armor or made by the same method.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-21:96\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The other passage names the force that the pass community fears: after its opening, Gog and Magog stream down, giving a cross-surah outcome to the threat named before the focus.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:94\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ يَأْجُوجَ وَمَأْجُوجَ مُفْسِدُونَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:98\",\"ar\":\"فَإِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ رَبِّى جَعَلَهُۥ دَكَّآءَ\"},{\"ref\":\"21:96\",\"ar\":\"حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فُتِحَتْ يَأْجُوجُ وَمَأْجُوجُ وَهُم مِّن كُلِّ حَدَبٍۢ يَنسِلُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus belongs to the construction scene that begins with the people’s explicit naming of Gog and Magog.\",\"limits\":\"21:96 does not mention the barrier or state that its opening is identical to the flattening in 18:98.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-22:21\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The focus turns iron and molten metal toward defense, while 22:20–21 place heated substance and iron clubs in a scene of punishment; the shared materials carry opposite functions.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"جَعَلَهُۥ نَارًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"قِطْرًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"22:20\",\"ar\":\"يُصْهَرُ بِهِۦ مَا فِى بُطُونِهِمْ وَٱلْجُلُودُ\"},{\"ref\":\"22:21\",\"ar\":\"وَلَهُم مَّقَٰمِعُ مِنْ حَدِيدٍۢ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s fire, iron, and molten metal make the punitive scene’s material vocabulary audible in a different use.\",\"limits\":\"The verses do not equate the focus’s fire with hellfire or describe the same objects or participants.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-22:40\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The focus’s collective labor can be heard beside the Quranic pattern of people checking one another to prevent destruction: the community supplies strength for protection, and Dhū al-Qarnayn credits his capacity to his Lord.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"مَا مَكَّنِّى فِيهِ رَبِّى خَيْرٌۭ فَأَعِينُونِى بِقُوَّةٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"22:40\",\"ar\":\"وَلَوْلَا دَفْعُ ٱللَّهِ ٱلنَّاسَ بَعْضَهُم بِبَعْضٍۢ لَّهُدِّمَتْ\"}],\"activation\":\"The people’s assistance and the barrier’s protective purpose give the focus a humanly enacted form of restraint.\",\"limits\":\"22:40 discusses protection of worship places and does not mention this barrier, its builders, or Gog and Magog.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-23:13\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-23:27\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The Ark and the pass barrier are both protective works made through organized construction, though one is built by divine instruction and the other in response to a people’s request.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"23:27\",\"ar\":\"فَأَوْحَيْنَآ إِلَيْهِ أَنِ ٱصْنَعِ ٱلْفُلْكَ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:94\",\"ar\":\"فَهَلْ نَجْعَلُ لَكَ خَرْجًا عَلَىٰٓ أَن تَجْعَلَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَهُمْ سَدًّۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"ءَاتُونِى زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both scenes describe a constructed defense against a threat to a community.\",\"limits\":\"The passages use different materials, builders, and directives; the focus does not explicitly mention revelation.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-23:53\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"زُبَرَ in the focus names iron pieces mobilized for a barrier, while زُبُرًا in 23:53 describes people splitting their affair into portions; the wording invites a contrast between pieces put to a common defensive work and a community divided among itself.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ\"},{\"ref\":\"23:53\",\"ar\":\"فَتَقَطَّعُوٓا۟ أَمْرَهُم بَيْنَهُمْ زُبُرًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The repeated noun form زبر appears in both passages, with iron specified in the focus and a divided affair in 23:53.\",\"limits\":\"The verses do not state that the focus intentionally echoes 23:53, and their collocations give the word distinct contextual senses.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-23:99\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-23:100\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The focus’s barrier is temporary until the Lord’s promise; 23:100 also gives a boundary a defined term, lasting until the day people are raised.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:98\",\"ar\":\"فَإِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ رَبِّى جَعَلَهُۥ دَكَّآءَ\"},{\"ref\":\"23:100\",\"ar\":\"وَمِن وَرَآئِهِم بَرْزَخٌ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages mark a boundary by the event or time at which its term ends.\",\"limits\":\"The barzakh is not identified with the built barrier, and the passages describe different settings and events.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-25:53\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The clause جَعَلَ بَيْنَهُمَا بَرْزَخًا parallels Dhū al-Qarnayn’s promise أَجْعَلْ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ رَدْمًا: both frame boundary-making as placing a separation between two parties.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"25:53\",\"ar\":\"وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَهُمَا بَرْزَخًۭا وَحِجْرًۭا مَّحْجُورًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"أَجْعَلْ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ رَدْمًا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:98\",\"ar\":\"هَٰذَا رَحْمَةٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّى\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus describes a barrier between threatened people and their attackers and calls it mercy from the Lord.\",\"limits\":\"25:53 describes waters and does not attribute the boundary to human construction; the verses do not state that Dhū al-Qarnayn imitates it.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-26:42\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-26:128\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The focus’s rدم answers a specified danger at one pass, contrasting with the questioned building of an ayah at every height for play.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"26:128\",\"ar\":\"أَتَبْنُونَ بِكُلِّ رِيعٍ ءَايَةًۭ تَعْبَثُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:94\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ يَأْجُوجَ وَمَأْجُوجَ مُفْسِدُونَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"أَجْعَلْ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ رَدْمًا\"}],\"activation\":\"The local people identify a concrete threat and request a barrier before construction begins.\",\"limits\":\"The verses do not use the same construction terms or explicitly compare the builders’ motives.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-26:129\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The expectation of living forever through constructed strongholds contrasts with Dhū al-Qarnayn’s explicit admission that his barrier will be flattened when the Lord’s promise arrives.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"26:129\",\"ar\":\"وَتَتَّخِذُونَ مَصَانِعَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَخْلُدُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:98\",\"ar\":\"فَإِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ رَبِّى جَعَلَهُۥ دَكَّآءَ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages put human construction beside claims about duration, but only the focus explicitly subordinates the structure to a divine term.\",\"limits\":\"The verses do not identify the structures or builders as the same, and the focus does not state that its barrier was intended to last forever.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-26:177\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-26:185\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-26:196\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ in the focus and زُبُرِ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ in 26:196 share the noun form but occur with different specifying phrases, one for iron and one for earlier peoples.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ\"},{\"ref\":\"26:196\",\"ar\":\"فِى زُبُرِ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"23:53\",\"ar\":\"أَمْرَهُم بَيْنَهُمْ زُبُرًۭا\"}],\"missing\":\"A dictionary account of زبر and its Quranic usage could establish whether the contexts share a semantic association beyond the form, or whether the similarity is only formal.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-26:226\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-27:7\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Moses seeks a fire for news or warmth, while Dhū al-Qarnayn directs blowing to bring iron to a fire-state; the shared نار contrasts a sought source of comfort with controlled heat for construction.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"27:7\",\"ar\":\"إِنِّىٓ ءَانَسْتُ نَارًۭا سَـَٔاتِيكُم مِّنْهَا بِخَبَرٍ أَوْ ءَاتِيكُم بِشِهَابٍۢ قَبَسٍۢ لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَصْطَلُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"قَالَ ٱنفُخُوا۟\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"جَعَلَهُۥ نَارًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus explicitly orders plural blowing and names the heated material as نارًا.\",\"limits\":\"The passages depict different people, purposes, and fires; 27:7 and 28:29 recount the same fire episode rather than independent ones.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-27:31\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-27:61\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The focus’s engineered rدم occupies a pass between paired sides; 27:61 places a حاجز between seas among the features that make the earth stable and ordered.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"27:61\",\"ar\":\"أَن تَقُومَ ٱلْأَرْضُ قَرَارًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"27:61\",\"ar\":\"وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَ ٱلْبَحْرَيْنِ حَاجِزًا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"أَجْعَلْ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ رَدْمًا\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages use جعل بين to describe a separating boundary, and the focus places its barrier in a mountain pass.\",\"limits\":\"27:61 describes a divine boundary in the earth; it does not say that Dhū al-Qarnayn’s construction reproduces that act.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-28:10\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-28:29\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"same-as:R-27:7\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-28:38\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Pharaoh orders fire kindled on clay before commanding a lofty structure; the focus also joins directed fire-work and construction, but applies it to a communal defense rather than Pharaoh’s self-exalting project.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"28:38\",\"ar\":\"فَأَوْقِدْ لِى يَٰهَٰمَٰنُ عَلَى ٱلطِّينِ فَٱجْعَل لِّى صَرْحًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"28:39\",\"ar\":\"وَٱسْتَكْبَرَ هُوَ وَجُنُودُهُۥ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ ٱلْحَقِّ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"قَالَ ٱنفُخُوا۟\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages place a ruler’s command, fire, and construction together; the focus supplies its defensive purpose in the surrounding verses.\",\"limits\":\"The verses do not describe identical materials or say Pharaoh’s fire-work serves the same engineering function as the focus’s heating stage.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-29:30\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The prayer for aid against القوم المفسدين shares the corruption root with the people’s description of Gog and Magog as مفسدون; Dhū al-Qarnayn answers such a threat by accepting their assistance and building a barrier.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"29:30\",\"ar\":\"قَالَ رَبِّ ٱنصُرْنِى عَلَى ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلْمُفْسِدِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:94\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ يَأْجُوجَ وَمَأْجُوجَ مُفْسِدُونَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"فَأَعِينُونِى بِقُوَّةٍ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names the threatened group as corrupters and contains a direct request for strength.\",\"limits\":\"The speakers and communities differ, and 29:30 is a prayer to God rather than a construction plan.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-30:25\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-32:13\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-33:14\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The imagined entry through a city’s outskirts and the claim that homes are exposed offer a defensive-space contrast to Dhū al-Qarnayn’s sealing of a specific pass so attackers cannot climb or pierce it.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"33:13\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ بُيُوتَنَا عَوْرَةٌۭ\"},{\"ref\":\"33:14\",\"ar\":\"وَلَوْ دُخِلَتْ عَلَيْهِم مِّنْ أَقْطَارِهَا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"أَجْعَلْ بَيْنَكُمْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ رَدْمًا\"},{\"ref\":\"18:97\",\"ar\":\"وَمَا ٱسْتَطَٰعُوا۟ لَهُۥ نَقْبًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages make the vulnerability or protection of a population legible through the spaces through which attackers might enter.\",\"limits\":\"33:14 describes a hypothetical entry and does not mention a barrier like the one in the focus.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-33:19\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-33:26\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The people brought down from their fortresses show that defensive strongholds do not guarantee protection; the focus likewise gives its barrier a fixed limit, ending when the Lord’s promise comes.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"33:26\",\"ar\":\"وَأَنزَلَ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَٰهَرُوهُم مِّنْ أَهْلِ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ مِن صَيَاصِيهِمْ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:98\",\"ar\":\"فَإِذَا جَآءَ وَعْدُ رَبِّى جَعَلَهُۥ دَكَّآءَ\"}],\"missing\":\"33:26 does not describe how the fortresses failed or link their defeat to the focus’s barrier. A passage specifying the means of their defeat or explicitly contrasting these defenses could establish the connection.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-34:10\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The focus’s use of iron follows a Quranic pattern of ironwork as a Lord-enabled capacity: David receives فضلًا and iron is made pliable for him, while Dhū al-Qarnayn says his Lord’s enablement is better.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"34:10\",\"ar\":\"وَلَقَدْ ءَاتَيْنَا دَاوُۥدَ مِنَّا فَضْلًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"34:10\",\"ar\":\"وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ ٱلْحَدِيدَ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:95\",\"ar\":\"مَا مَكَّنِّى فِيهِ رَبِّى خَيْرٌۭ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names iron as its principal material and explicitly credits the Lord with enabling Dhū al-Qarnayn.\",\"limits\":\"The passages describe different rulers and different ironworking; the focus does not say its iron was softened as David’s was.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-34:11\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"David’s protective craft is wearable, while Dhū al-Qarnayn’s is landscape-scale: both turn skilled work into protection from external force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"34:11\",\"ar\":\"أَنِ ٱعْمَلْ سَٰبِغَٰتٍۢ وَقَدِّرْ فِى ٱلسَّرْدِ\"},{\"ref\":\"21:80\",\"ar\":\"صَنْعَةَ لَبُوسٍۢ لَّكُمْ لِتُحْصِنَكُم مِّنۢ بَأْسِكُمْ\"},{\"ref\":\"18:96\",\"ar\":\"ءَاتُونِى زُبَرَ ٱلْحَدِيدِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both scenes join practical manufacture with defensive use; 21:80 states the armor’s protective purpose explicitly.\",\"limits\":\"The focus does not call the barrier armor or describe the same technique used for David’s work.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
